data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with native-sized integers.** Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

This compiled and ran successfully. The one caveat is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context (since the size isn't fixed at compile time), but `stackalloc` itself works fine in safe code when assigned directly to a `Span<T>`. On this 64-bit system, `nint` is 8 bytes.
